_V208_HEKA_HELP = ("HEKA ElProScan / PotMaster", r"""
HEKA DAT2 IMPORT AND HIERARCHY

FaradaIQ v273 reads a HEKA DAT2 file as a bundle, not as a flat current-time file. The browser preserves:
File > Group > technique/experiment > point > Series > Sweep/cycle > processed view.

What is decoded
• DAT2 bundle header and section table with checked offsets and lengths.
• PUL tree magic, byte order, hierarchy depth, and record sizes stored in the file.
• Root, Group, Series, Sweep, and Trace titles and acquisition order.
• Per-trace sample format, endian flag, scale, zero offset, X start, X increment, units, data offset, and sample count.
• Optional sections are indexed and preserved. Unsupported structures are reported without blocking usable traces.

Technique evidence
Classification combines Group/Series/Sweep/Trace names, units, current/potential monitor pairing, waveform direction and closure, processed Real(Z)/Imag(Z) channels, frequency excitation, spatial scan context, and parent/child structure. Confidence and evidence are exported for every Series. Uncertain Series remain Unknown HEKA.

CV, LSV, AND FSCV EXAMPLE
1. Load the .dat bundle and open Data browser + analysis.
2. Expand HEKA, the Group, then CV/LSV and the spatial point.
3. Select one or more Sweeps and choose Plot/overlay selected.
4. Auto mode uses current_A versus potential_V. Time remains available as an alternative X axis.
5. Repeated Sweeps remain under the original Series and retain cycle order.
A closing triangular waveform supports CV. A predominantly one-way ORR/polarization waveform supports LSV. A fastCV/FSCV protocol title supports FSCV.

EIS EXAMPLE
Processed Real(Z) and Imag(Z) channels are required for an EIS assignment. Imon/Emon oscillations alone are retained only as diagnostics. FaradaIQ assembles one spectrum per HEKA Group, with each EIS Series contributing one frequency point. Frequency is read from a channel when available or estimated from the excitation trace and X increment. The stored Zimag sign is preserved; neg_Zimag_ohm is added for conventional Nyquist display.

SPATIAL AND PROBE EXAMPLE
SECCM, SECM, SICM, shear-force, TipDown/PullUp, X/Y/Z scans, line scans, 2D matrices, 3D scans, and distance calibration retain acquisition order and hierarchy. When explicit coordinates cannot be decoded safely, FaradaIQ shows an ordered point list and writes a coordinate-status warning rather than inventing positions.

EXPORT CONTENTS
Each HEKA export includes hierarchy JSON, metadata JSON, technique evidence CSV/JSON, warnings, unsupported-section inventory, trace index, cycle assignments, spatial point table, technique-specific CSVs, Group-level EIS spectra, source SHA-256, and one compressed raw-trace HDF5 file. The *_heka_v210_manifest.json file is the reload contract used by the canonical H5/JSON builder.

TROUBLESHOOTING
• Unsupported version: inspect the parser warning and bundle version. Raw sections remain preserved.
• Missing optional section: usable PUL/DAT data still load; the missing section is listed.
• Inconsistent unit: label and context are shown with a warning. FaradaIQ does not silently swap axes.
• Incomplete coordinates: use ordered points; do not interpret them as a fabricated map.
• Partial EIS Group: incomplete frequency/Z rows are reported and excluded from a clean DRT handoff.
• Large file: parsing and export run through the existing background workflow. Do not start a duplicate export while the current transaction is active.
""")
