_V209_HEKA_HELP = ("HEKA complete semantics", r"""
HEKA PGF AND ONL COMPLETE SEMANTIC DECODING

FaradaIQ Studio v273 fully decodes the exact HEKA record versions contained in the attached ElProScan/PotMaster archive. This is not string scraping. Each file is read as a checked HEKA tree using its stored byte order, hierarchy depth, record sizes, child counts, and exact binary field offsets.

SUPPORTED ATTACHED RECORD LAYOUTS
• PGF stimulus tree v1000: Root 1144 bytes, Stimulation 248 bytes, Channel 400 bytes, Segment 80 bytes.
• ONL online-analysis tree v11: Root 64 bytes, Method 2640 bytes, Function 168 bytes.
• AMP amplifier-state tree v1000: Root 80 bytes, Series 16 bytes, State 560 bytes.
• SOL solution database v1000: Root 88 bytes, Solution 160 bytes, Chemical 40 bytes.
• MRK marker tree v9: Root 8 bytes, Marker 104 bytes.
• The fixed-length MTH EIS records used in the supplied training bundle.

PGF CONTENT THAT IS NOW DECODED
The parser exposes every documented root parameter and parameter label, stimulation name, source file, linked ONL analysis name, sample and sweep intervals, sweep/leak/average counts, acquisition and trigger flags, auto-ranging mode, lock-in and chirp settings, ADC and DAC channel configuration, physical units, holding values, compression and leak settings, sine/square/chirp settings, offsets, trace-math expression, break settings, segment class, store mode, voltage and duration sources, increment modes, voltage, duration, increments, scan rate, CRC values, reserved bytes, record offsets, and SHA-256 values.

PGF PROTOCOL RECONSTRUCTION
FaradaIQ reconstructs each sweep and segment in acquisition order. For every segment it reports the waveform class, voltage, duration, source semantics, increment semantics, start/end time, and scan rate. Explicit PGF evidence is linked to the matching PUL Series through each Sweep's stimulation index. For EIS, chSine_Cycle is interpreted as the attached protocol's sine period and converted to frequency. Stored frequency channels still take precedence when present.

ONL CONTENT THAT IS NOW DECODED
Every method includes all 12 graph definitions, active/overlay/wrap/normalization settings, X and Y scaling records, four graph entries, headers, saved axis ranges, CRC and reserved fields. Every function includes its name, unit, left/right operands, bounds, constant, segment offsets, enumerator, one of the documented 116 function types, notebook/fit/name flags, target and source values, cursor semantics, equation, baseline mode, search direction, anchor, CRC, record offset, and SHA-256.

SERIES AND ANALYSIS LINKING
PUL Sweep stimulation indices link recorded Series to PGF stimulations. PGF analysis names link those stimulations to ONL methods. The metadata panel and exported technique-evidence files therefore show the recorded Series, stimulation definition, reconstructed protocol, online method, and online functions together.

EXPORT EXAMPLE
Load a DAT2 bundle, select Export archive + CSV, then open:
  <source>_HEKA_v216/semantic_sections/
The folder contains complete JSON plus flat CSV tables for PGF stimulations, channels, segments, reconstructed sweep protocols, ONL methods, functions, graphs, and graph entries. AMP, SOL, MRK, and MTH semantics are also exported as complete JSON. Raw embedded bytes and checksums remain available for independent verification.

VALIDATION AND UNKNOWN VALUES
v216 accounts for every byte in the attached PGF and ONL trees and rejects truncated, overlong, or wrong-sized trees. One attached PGF field uses undocumented BreakMode code 3. FaradaIQ does not invent a name for it. It reports VendorExtension(BreakMode=3), preserves the raw code and record bytes, and continues safely. This is full decoding of all documented semantics plus exact preservation of the vendor extension.
""")
